WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.299
Ever since the first Zombieland staggered
into theaters in 2009, fans have clamored

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.180
for a sequel.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:11.420
We had to wait a full decade for a follow-up,
but from new zombies to every major storyline

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:15.980
in this long-awaited sequel, here's everything
you need to know about the ending of Zombieland:

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:16.640
Double Tap.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:22.560
As the film opens, we find our four main heroes
making their way to a new yet entirely familiar

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.320
home: an abandoned White House.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.140
They spend a little time being a dysfunctional
family, then hit the road again after Little

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.520
Rock runs off with a pacifist named Berkeley.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.100
Along the way, they kill a bunch of zombies,
meet some new friends, get up to some Elvis

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.700
shenanigans, and have a short-lived run-in
with a couple doppelgangers.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.760
“Oh, God, those are T-800s, or at the very
least T-700s.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.480
There actually was no T-700.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.900
Yeah, T-800's the first model.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.740
It's great having two of you."

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:53.320
Things get back on track after Nevada, the
proprietor of the Hound Dog Hotel, tells the

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.400
group that she saw Little Rock and Berkeley
and knows where they're going.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.060
This all leads up to the gang heading to Babylon,
a commune which promotes a pacifist way of

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:01.560
life.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.720
It's mostly just filled with twenty-somethings
doing the world's last remaining drugs and

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:09.510
playing hacky sack, despite the hordes of
zombies that have taken over the planet.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.180
"No worries, man.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:12.980
No, there's some worries, man.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:14.860
There's some worries."

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:19.560
As the gang sets off, they end up finding
a familiar and fairly unwelcome face on the

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:24.840
road: the very bubbly, very ditzy Madison,
who everybody thought got shot earlier in

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:25.380
the film.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.679
As it turns out, Columbus didn't actually
shoot Madison.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.320
She never even became a zombie at all — she
was just allergic to trail mix.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.540
With Madison in tow, the gang finally finds
their way to Babylon, a seemingly successful

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:42.220
stronghold complete with an enormous tower
that's protected by walls on all sides.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:46.600
Much to the gang's dismay, guns are confiscated
and melted down at Babylon.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.780
After reuniting with Little Rock, the gang
realizes that she's happy being with friends

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:54.700
her own age, and they all realize they need
to give her a little room to live her life.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:59.100
Tallahassee, who has been itching to return
to the road for the entire film, decides to

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.640
leave Babylon and set off on his own once
more.

00:02:01.889 --> 00:02:06.960
But as he drives away, he notices a ton of
super-fast zombies heading right for Babylon,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.640
which is, of course, setting off fireworks
and playing music as loudly as possible.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:16.100
Tallahassee reverses course immediately and
returns to Babylon, warning its inhabitants

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:20.230
as he tries to figure out a course of action
to defend the complex considering there are

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.970
absolutely zero weapons on the premises.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:27.520
Eventually, they come up with a solution involving
plenty of biofuel and fire.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.420
It seems to work...until it doesn't.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:34.160
The four heroes find themselves surrounded
by zombies, thinking the end has finally come.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:38.700
In the end, Double Tap doesn't dispose of
its four main characters during their final

00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:43.760
showdown; at the last second, a monster truck,
driven by Nevada, arrives to mow down as many

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.120
zombies as possible.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:49.159
Once they all pile in, they return to Babylon,
where the weakened residents are attempting

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.920
to barricade themselves against hordes of
vicious, superfast undead.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:57.800
Tallahassee's plan, as it turns out, left
no stone unturned, thanks in part to his newfound

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.300
heritage.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:03.280
Early in the film, he bores Columbus with
an explanation about his Native American bloodline,

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:07.740
rattling off a long story about Native American
hunters luring buffalo off of a cliff.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.140
Since nothing in the Zombieland films ever
happens by accident, it seems inevitable that

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.560
this story would end up serving an important
purpose.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:15.980
Naturally, it does.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:20.440
As Tallahassee lures the zombies upstairs,
it turns out they have a trap laid on top

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:21.980
of Babylon's highest tower.

00:03:22.189 --> 00:03:26.840
For a moment it seems like Zombieland's toughest
hero might fall, but his littlest friend comes

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:27.540
to his aid.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:33.080
Babylon might not allow any guns, but Little
Rock snuck one in; specifically, Elvis' gun

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:37.590
that Tallahassee gave to her for Christmas,
which she uses to shoot the last of the zombie

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.420
horde and save Tallahassee's life.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.560
In the aftermath of the massive zombie attack
on Babylon, several characters come back together

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.560
for happy endings.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:49.960
Tallahassee and Nevada reunite, and with Little
Rock's blessing, Madison and Berkeley pair

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:50.460
off.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:55.600
Most importantly, Wichita turns to Columbus
and says the only word she needs to say — "yes"

00:03:55.609 --> 00:04:00.430
— and the two officially get engaged, despite
Wichita's misgivings about marriage and the

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:01.580
pair's recent split.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.920
Along with Nevada, the gang drives off in
Elvis Presley's pink Cadillac, with their

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:07.860
destination completely unknown.

00:04:08.249 --> 00:04:13.019
When asked where they should go together,
Columbus simply says, "home," ultimately elaborating

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:16.020
that, with his chosen family, home can be
anywhere in the world.

00:04:16.109 --> 00:04:19.959
It might seem odd for a zombie movie to have
such a happy ending, but that's simply the

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:24.419
Zombieland style: it lets its heroes have
everything they want, even as the world around

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:25.479
them crumbles.

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.660
"They were the closest to something I'd always
wanted, but never really had.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.240
A family."

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:37.160
Of course, no Zombieland film would be complete
without a celebrity cameo, particularly after

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.060
the first film's Bill Murray guest spot.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:43.040
Naturally, Murray comes up pretty quickly
in the film; shortly after the gang meets

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:47.800
Nevada, she says she almost "Murrayed" Tallahassee,
explaining that shooting a human you think

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:52.110
might be a zombie is called "Murraying," thanks
to the little case of mistaken identity that

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:53.420
happened in the first film.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.199
"Is that how you say hello where you come
from?"

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.660
"Oh my God, oh my God I can't believe I shot
Bill Murray."

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.020
During the credits, Columbus gives the audience
a glimpse at Murray's first day in the zombie

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:10.830
apocalypse, which initially finds him conducting
unenthusiastic press interviews for the fictional

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.840
Garfield 3: Flabby Tabby.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:17.480
After Al Roker succumbs to the zombie infection,
Murray mows his way through a press room,

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:22.260
gleefully taking out zombies while quoting
everything from Ghostbusters to Caddyshack

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.400
to, well, Garfield.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.620
"I hate Mondays.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:25.680
Just hate 'em."

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.900
The ending of Double Tap sees our heroes literally
riding off into the sunset.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:33.930
But as with the first film, which ended in
a pretty similar way, the movie definitely

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.580
leaves the door open for a possible third
Zombieland.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:40.960
However, after a ten-year wait between the
first Zombieland film and its sequel, it also

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.380
seems as if assembling the teams on either
side of the camera might be a pretty Herculean

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:45.880
task.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:50.500
Emma Stone, Woody Harrelson, Abigail Breslin,
and Jesse Eisenberg are all more in demand

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:55.030
than ever, and writers Rhett Reese and Paul
Wernick have been involved in a ton of high-profile

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:57.780
projects since they made a splash with the
first Zombieland.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:02.479
With that said, zombie stories are always
an extraordinarily rich creative well, so

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:06.880
a third Zombieland film would likely not only
be well-received, but well-attended to boot.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.599
If Double Tap closes out this witty, clever
series, its ending serves as a perfect coda

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.360
to this extremely fun saga.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.500
But if the demand is there for it, there are
definitely still more stories to experience

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:22.320
alongside Columbus, Tallahassee, Wichita,
Little Rock, and their new friend Nevada.

